        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Delete a sub-object (line, condition, etc.) from its parent document.\n
\n
    Uses ERP5\'s Base_deleteObject which either physically removes the object\n
    (if it has no workflow history) or transitions it to \'deleted\' state.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need to remove a sub-object like a Sale Order Line, Payment Condition, etc.\n
    - The sub-object was created by mistake or is no longer needed.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You want to delete/cancel a top-level document — use erp5_action with\n
      \'cancel_action\' or \'delete_action\' instead.\n
    - You want to edit fields — use erp5_write instead.\n
\n
    PREREQUISITE: Call erp5_read on the parent to see sub-objects, then identify the\n
    relative_url of the sub-object to delete.\n
    </string> </value>
